# shadcn/ui (investor-onboarding)

This app has shadcn configured (`apps/investor-onboarding/components.json`). Prefer [shadcn components](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) over custom-styled native elements for forms, inputs, dialogs, etc.

## Add components

From `apps/investor-onboarding`:

```bash
pnpm exec shadcn add <component> --yes
```

Examples: `input`, `checkbox`, `label`, `field`, `select`, `card`.

## Use components

Import from `@/components/ui/<name>` (e.g. `Button`, `Input`, `Checkbox`, `Label`). Check `src/components/ui/` for what is already installed before adding duplicates.

## When to deviate

Use plain HTML or one-off Tailwind only when no shadcn primitive fits and adding a component would be heavier than the use case.
